.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 
Represents a optional value container that stores a value only when \fBHasValue\fP is true\&. Unlike Nullable<T>, this type does not preserve \fRnull\fP as a stored value; assigning \fRnull\fP clears the optional state\&. 


.PP
\fBTemplate Parameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIT\fP The underlying value type\&. Can be either a reference type or a value type\&. 
.RE
.PP

