.SS "\fBCompareResult\fP SystemEx\&.Optional< T >\&.CompareTo (\fBOptional\fP< T > other)"

.PP
Compares this optional instance with another optional instance and returns a \fBCompareResult\fP describing their relative ordering\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIother\fP The optional instance to compare against\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
A \fBCompareResult\fP value indicating whether this instance is less than, equal to, or greater than the specified instance\&. 
.RE
.PP

.PP
Comparison rules: 
.PD 0
.IP "\(bu" 2
An empty optional (\fBHasValue\fP is \fRfalse\fP) is always considered greater than a non‑empty optional, ensuring that empty values sort last\&.  
.IP "\(bu" 2
If both optionals are empty, they are considered equal\&.  
.IP "\(bu" 2
If both contain values, the comparison is performed using Comparer<T>\&.Default and the result is cast directly to \fBCompareResult\fP\&.  
.PP

